{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-84cfca80-f569-44a9-85b9-3bc18b56ec00","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c104f965e428a57","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-rejgii7z/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md","content":"# FIPS remediation of KServe and serving data plane images\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic removes non-validated cryptographic module usage from the KServe component images and the serving data plane images so that the model serving stack runs correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters with no non-validated crypto in the request path. It produces the module inventory and remediation records that the compliance evidence package is assembled from.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit every KServe component image and serving data plane image for linkages to non-validated cryptographic libraries (including transitive dependencies), recording findings as a module inventory (image, library, version, validation status).\n- Remediate each finding: rebuild or rebase images so the request path links only validated cryptographic modules.\n- Carry required changes in the midstream KServe repositories; upstream contributions only where a change cannot be carried midstream.\n- Functionally verify remediated images on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster in both serverless and raw deployment modes (the two supported deployment modes per the architecture context).\n- Deliver the module inventory and remediation records for use by the compliance evidence package.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A module inventory covering every KServe component and serving data plane image exists, listing each cryptographic library linkage and its validation status.\n- A scan of the remediated images confirms no non-validated cryptographic module is linked in the request path of any serving-stack image.\n- Remediated images pass functional verification of the inference request path on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster, in both serverless and raw deployment modes.\n- Each remediated image build is revertible to the prior build (documented rollback path), since this work replaces existing image builds.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the request path) — this epic delivers that for the KServe components and the serving data plane.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43646,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9536c0861243fc4","agent_id":"ab2915676e1df60fa","session_id":"b1b2271b-4c69-47a7-906c-4aa2a3507a54","uuid":"8f7b3308-46f7-4621-8373-385f7686d5cd","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:47:26.259Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
