{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-bae34a92-b703-4cd2-be45-f1a0b6ddbe5d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7455012ee4077cc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-rejgii7z/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E003.md","content":"# Compliance evidence package and certification submission\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic assembles the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model serving stack — module inventory, build attestations, and test results — and steers it through the mandatory security review board milestones to submission at the external accredited certification laboratory.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Consolidate the module inventories, remediation records, and FIPS functional test results produced by the serving-stack image remediation (KServe components, serving data plane) and the Platform Operator compliance work.\n- Collect build attestations from the serving-stack build pipelines for every image in scope.\n- Assemble the evidence package in the format required by the certification process.\n- Submit the package through the security review board at the defined milestones, triaging and addressing board feedback.\n- Submit the package to the external accredited certification laboratory and record its intake status.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The evidence package contains the module inventory, build attestations, and test results for every serving-stack image in scope (KServe components, serving data plane, and Platform Operator).\n- The evidence package is submitted to the security review board at each defined milestone, and board feedback is triaged and addressed.\n- The evidence package is submitted to the external accredited certification laboratory, and its intake/triage status is recorded.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Certification laboratory turnaround is historically six to nine months, and review-board cadence is externally controlled; neither can be compressed by engineering effort. These are schedule risks, not acceptance conditions — the epic's engineering completion point is the assembled, submitted, and triaged package.\n- The certification outcome and its timing are outside this strategy's control; the engineering compliance value (FIPS-capable images, CI enforcement, documentation) does not depend on it.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44764,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9536c0861243fc4","agent_id":"ab2915676e1df60fa","session_id":"b1b2271b-4c69-47a7-906c-4aa2a3507a54","uuid":"238a7b94-f4c7-4a21-8d3e-138dacb1d947","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:47:38.223Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
