{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8689a6e6705982e1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: FIPS remediation of KServe and serving data plane images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS remediation of KServe and serving data plane images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic removes non-validated cryptographic module usage from the KServe component images and the serving data plane images so that the model serving stack runs correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters with no non-validated crypto in the request path. It produces the module inventory and remediation records that the compliance evidence package is assembled from.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Audit every KServe component image and serving data plane image for linkages to non-validated cryptographic libraries (including transitive dependencies), recording findings as a module inventory (image, library, version, validation status).\n38\t- Remediate each finding: rebuild or rebase images so the request path links only validated cryptographic modules.\n39\t- Carry required changes in the midstream KServe repositories; upstream contributions only where a change cannot be carried midstream.\n40\t- Functionally verify remediated images on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster in both serverless and raw deployment modes (the two supported deployment modes per the architecture context).\n41\t- Deliver the module inventory and remediation records for use by the compliance evidence package.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- A module inventory covering every KServe component and serving data plane image exists, listing each cryptographic library linkage and its validation status.\n46\t- A scan of the remediated images confirms no non-validated cryptographic module is linked in the request path of any serving-stack image.\n47\t- Remediated images pass functional verification of the inference request path on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster, in both serverless and raw deployment modes.\n48\t- Each remediated image build is revertible to the prior build (documented rollback path), since this work replaces existing image builds.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the request path) — this epic delivers that for the KServe components and the serving data plane.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c1fd37fcb0dc5ac","agent_id":"ab9d6186626e0d028","session_id":"b1b2271b-4c69-47a7-906c-4aa2a3507a54","uuid":"896f196a-860e-4d42-b923-2f360a891421","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:49:30.226Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8689a6e6705982e1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
