{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a112c3463482dec6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9013\n3\tscore: 12\n4\tpass: false\n5\trecommendation: revise\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: critical\n8\t  criterion: DAG Coherence\n9\t  description: 'E002 scope and AC consume E001 artifact with no DAG edge: E002 verifies\n10\t    the operator deploys the serving stack (including the FIPS-remediated serving\n11\t    images; AC requires CR Ready for an InferenceService using remediated images)\n12\t    but has dependencies: [] and the summary claims E001/E002 share no artifacts.\n13\t    Add edge E001 -> E002 or reword E002 verification to not require E001 remediated\n14\t    images.'\n15\t- severity: minor\n16\t  criterion: Epic Boundaries\n17\t  description: E003 and E004 span Platform Operator work but carry component KServe\n18\t    (single-component schema field); acknowledged in Component Mapping Notes, acceptable.\n19\terror: null\n20\t---\n21\t# Decomposition Review — RHAISTRAT-9013\n22\t\n23\t## Review Summary\n24\t\n25\tScore: 12/14 — fail\n26\tRecommendation: revise\n27\t\n28\tContract validator: OK (all mechanical checks passed: body sections, canonical\n29\tcomponent names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority inheritance,\n30\timplementation-type parallelism).\n31\t\n32\tTriage consistency: `triage: null` (full decomposition) with 5 epics —\n33\tmulti-epic output is expected; no contradiction.\n34\t\n35\tOne critical issue forces Criterion 2 to 0, which triggers the auto-fail rule\n36\tregardless of the total score.\n37\t\n38\t## Criterion Details\n39\t\n40\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n41\tAll four HLRs map to epics: HLR-1 → E001 + E002, HLR-2 → E003, HLR-3 → E004,\n42\tHLR-4 → E005. Traceability matrix is present and matches each epic's HLR\n43\tTraceability section. Priority inheritance is correct: E003 (P0) is blocked\n44\tonly by P0 epics; E004 (P1) blocks no P0 work; E005 is a docs-authoring epic\n45\texempt from priority inheritance (P0 via the strategy's Critical priority, per\n46\trule). No priority collapse — each epic maps to exactly one HLR, so deferrable\n47\tP1/P2 work (HLR-3, HLR-4) is independently plannable.\n48\t\n49\t### 2. DAG Coherence (0/2)\n50\tDiagram and frontmatter are mutually consistent (every arrow has a matching\n51\t`dependencies` entry and vice versa; arrows drawn dependency → dependent).\n52\tNo circular dependencies, no invalid references, no konflux/license/repo\n53\tonboarding types present so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is not implicated.\n54\tCritical path length 3 (E001 → E003 → E005) fits the M-strategy heuristic\n55\t(3-4).\n56\t\n57\tHowever, the cross-check of epic content against the DAG finds a missing\n58\tdata/artifact dependency: E002's scope bullet (\"Verify the operator deploys,\n59\treconciles, and manages the serving stack (including the FIPS-remediated\n60\tserving images)\") and its acceptance criterion (\"CR status reaches Ready for a\n61\tdeployed InferenceService using remediated images\") explicitly consume the\n62\tremediated serving images produced by E001 — yet E002 has `dependencies: []`\n63\tand the summary asserts E001/E002 share no artifacts. As written, E002's\n64\tverification AC cannot be satisfied if E002 runs before E001 completes. Either\n65\tthe edge E001 → E002 must be added, or E002's verification must be reworded to\n66\tverify operator reconciliation independently of the remediated image set (the\n67\toperator's own FIPS compliance does not inherently require E001's images).\n68\tThis is a critical issue per the content-cross-check rule (an epic consuming\n69\tan image produced by another epic with no edge to it), so this criterion\n70\tscores 0.\n71\t\n72\tAll other edges are justified: E001/E002 → E003 (Rule 13, evidence package\n73\tconsumes inventories/records/test results), E001/E002 → E004 (Rule 12/13, gate\n74\tbaseline derived from remediated image set), and the four Rule 11 docs-last\n75\tedges into E005.\n76\t\n77\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n78\tComponent/team tuples are cleanly separated: E001 (KServe) vs E002 (Platform\n79\tOperator) are separate epics under the same team; E003/E004/E005 each carry a\n80\tsingle logical change. No scope duplication — E001 and E002 audit/remediate\n81\tdisjoint image sets; E003 consolidates rather than rebuilds; E004 reuses\n82\tdetection criteria rather than re-deriving them. No work-product type mixing\n83\t(E003 is a process deliverable, not bundled code+content; E005 is pure\n84\tdocs-authoring). Epic sizes are plausible single-sprint-ish units.\n85\t\n86\tMinor (does not reduce score): E003 and E004 span Platform Operator work but\n87\tcarry `component: KServe` because the schema allows one canonical component;\n88\tthis is acknowledged and justified in the summary's Component Mapping Notes.\n89\t\n90\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n91\tAll five epics are Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact\n92\t(remediated images + inventory, operator compliance + test results, evidence\n93\tpackage, CI gate, published docs). No epic is misclassified: the audit inside\n94\tE001 is discovery within a fixed find-and-replace approach, not uncertainty\n95\tthat changes downstream structure, so no Investigation epic is required. No\n96\t`gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are set, and none are needed (no\n97\tInvestigation epics, no conditional branches).\n98\t\n99\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n100\tAll epics are Implementation and carry the 9-signal `ai_signals` field (no\n101\ttype mismatch). Signal values are consistent with the rubric and the\n102\tstrategy content, and each ai-signals file's rationale matches its frontmatter\n103\tvalue. Notably correct: `open_questions: 1` across epics (strategy states\n104\t\"None on scope\"); E002 `change_specificity: -1` (operator scope inferred, not\n105\tspecified); E003 `external_dependency: -1` / `human_process_gates: -1`\n106\t(external lab + review board); E002 `architecture_claims: 0` per the signal\n107\trule (no context file covers Platform Operator — flagged as a health warning,\n108\tcorrectly). The `architecture_claims: 1` scores on E001/E003/E004/E005 cite\n109\t`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`, which does\n110\tcorroborate the premises used (serving stack role, both deployment modes,\n111\tKonflux onboarding, serverless mesh dependency). No arithmetic checked\n112\t(pipeline-computed).\n113\t\n114\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n115\tEvery epic has testable ACs. Rule-mandated ACs are present: rollback paths on\n116\tboth replacement epics (E001, E002), technical-review AC on the docs-authoring\n117\tepic (E005), and an end-to-end gate-failure verification test on E004. E003\n118\tcorrectly moves the externally-controlled lab turnaround and review-board\n119\tcadence into Risks/Notes instead of ACs — exactly the soft-AC anti-pattern\n120\tavoided, with ACs written at the engineering completion point. No epic body\n121\treferences sibling epics by draft ID (prose refers to \"the compliance evidence\n122\tpackage\" / \"the image remediation audit\" by name, which is correct practice).\n123\t\n124\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n125\tFull strategy scope is covered: both P0 HLRs, the P1 CI gate, and the P2 docs\n126\twork all have epics; out-of-scope boundaries (workbenches/pipelines/training,\n127\tCommon Criteria) are respected and restated in E005. Strategy-level context is\n128\tcarried forward, not dropped: the external lab/review-board scheduling\n129\tconstraint from the Problem Statement and Open Questions appears in E003's\n130\tRisks/Notes and the summary's Health Warnings; the Serving Runtimes ambiguity\n131\tand unverified Platform Operator in-platform status are flagged as health\n132\twarnings. No conditional branches are used and none are needed (the strategy\n133\thas no bounded-outcome uncertainty). No docs-authoring Prerequisites section\n134\texists in the strategy, but HLR-4 mandates documentation and E005 fulfills it.\n135\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d5862fc1d390e01","agent_id":"a6daf208703aac9a7","session_id":"b1b2271b-4c69-47a7-906c-4aa2a3507a54","uuid":"94078b6f-563b-46d9-bd4f-22de8a8990c3","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:52:35.395Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a112c3463482dec6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
