{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad77371189845d80","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9013 (FIPS 140-3 compliance for the model serving stack)\n10\t\n11\t## Epic List\n12\t\n13\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n14\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n15\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E001 | FIPS remediation of KServe and serving data plane images | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n16\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 | Platform Operator FIPS compliance | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n17\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 | Compliance evidence package and certification submission | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n18\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 | CI gating check for FIPS regressions | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P1 |\n19\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E005 | FIPS support posture documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n20\t\n21\t## Dependency DAG\n22\t\n23\t```mermaid\n24\tgraph TD\n25\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9013-E001 KServe image FIPS remediation] --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 Evidence package and submission]\n26\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 Platform Operator FIPS compliance] --> E003\n27\t    E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 CI FIPS regression gate]\n28\t    E002 --> E004\n29\t    E001 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9013-E005 FIPS documentation]\n30\t    E002 --> E005\n31\t    E003 --> E005\n32\t    E004 --> E005\n33\t```\n34\t\n35\t## DAG Justification\n36\t\n37\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n38\t|------|------|-----------|\n39\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (artifact consumption) | The evidence package consumes the module inventory, remediation records, and FIPS test results produced by the image remediation; it cannot be assembled before those artifacts exist. |\n40\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (artifact consumption) | Same: the operator's remediation records and test results are inputs to the evidence package. |\n41\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 12/13 (builds against remediated state) | The gating check's pass/fail baseline is derived from the remediated image set; enabling the gate before remediation would fail every serving-stack build. |\n42\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 12/13 (builds against remediated state) | The gate covers all serving-stack builds including the platform operator's image builds, so the operator's baseline must be clean first. |\n43\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built. |\n44\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built. |\n45\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built, including the certification posture. |\n46\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built, including the regression-enforcement posture. |\n47\t\n48\tE001 and E002 have no edge between them: different components/repos, no shared artifacts (Rule 14 — parallel).\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n51\t\n52\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epic(s) |\n53\t|-----|----------|------------------------|---------|\n54\t| HLR-1 | P0 | All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules | RHAISTRAT-9013-E001, RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 |\n55\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Compliance evidence package assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab | RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 |\n56\t| HLR-3 | P1 | CI enforces FIPS regressions with a gating check | RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 |\n57\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation states the FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites | RHAISTRAT-9013-E005 |\n58\t\n59\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n60\t\n61\t## Component Mapping Notes\n62\t\n63\t- **KServe** is a canonical component (`.context/rhai-components.txt`) and has an architecture-context file (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`): Stable (GA), owning team RHOAI Serving, midstream `opendatahub-io/kserve`, Konflux-onboarded. E001, E003, and E004 are assigned component `KServe`.\n64\t- The strategy's phrase \"KServe components and the serving data plane\" is tracked under the single `KServe` component per the strategy's own Affected Components list. The serving data plane may overlap Serving Runtimes images (per the architecture context, KServe depends on Serving Runtimes for model execution); if remediation work lands in Serving Runtimes repos, the mapping should be revisited — flagged as a health warning below.\n65\t- **Platform Operator** is a canonical Jira component but has **no architecture-context file**. It is treated as an existing in-platform component (the strategy presumes a deployed operator managing the serving stack, and the component is in the canonical list) rather than triggering the new-component onboarding chain — the strategy's problem is non-validated crypto in existing images, not component provisioning. Its in-platform status is nonetheless unverified; flagged as a health warning.\n66\t- E004's gate spans all serving-stack build pipelines, including the platform operator's builds; the single most-relevant canonical name `KServe` is assigned and the span noted here.\n67\t- E005 is assigned component `Documentation` (canonical) for the docs-authoring work stream.\n68\t\n69\t## Health Warnings\n70\t\n71\t1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no per-component change/owner table (Affected Components is a bare list), no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements. Team assignments are inferred: `RHOAI Serving` for all epics, taken from the KServe architecture-context file (the only team data available). Platform Operator ownership is unverified.\n72\t2. **Platform Operator architecture context absent**: no file in `.context/architecture-context/` covers Platform Operator, so its architecture claims cannot be corroborated (signal 9 scored 0 for E002). If the operator is in fact not in the platform, this decomposition under-scopes provisioning work.\n73\t3. **Serving data plane scope ambiguity**: \"serving data plane\" images are tracked under KServe per the strategy's component list, but may involve Serving Runtimes-owned images. If so, a separate epic (component `Serving Runtimes`) should be spun out at execution time.\n74\t4. **Docs epic priority**: E005 carries P0 via the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0) even though its HLR-4 is P2. This is rule-mandated, does not propagate upstream (E004 correctly remains P1), and is noted here because it reads as an inversion against the HLR table.\n75\t5. **Possible priority inversion (HLR-3)**: the CI regression gate is P1 while it protects P0 compliance — a reintroduced non-validated-crypto regression could invalidate certification evidence already submitted. The strategy's P1 label is preserved, but reviewers may want to raise it.\n76\t6. **External schedule risk (not an AC)**: certification lab turnaround is historically six to nine months and review-board cadence is externally controlled; neither can be compressed by engineering effort. Recorded as Risks/Notes on E003, with ACs written at the engineering completion point (package assembled, submitted, triaged).\n77\t\n78\t## Tiered Delivery\n79\t\n80\tThe external certification process has uncertain timing; partial value does not depend on it:\n81\t\n82\t- **Tier 1 (independent value)**: E001, E002, E004 — FIPS-capable serving-stack images that run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters, plus CI regression enforcement. Deliverable and usable regardless of certification outcome timing.\n83\t- **Tier 2 (externally gated)**: E003 — evidence package submission through the security review board to the accredited lab; the submission is engineering-controlled but the certification outcome and its timing are not. E005 (documentation) follows the evidence work per the docs-last rule.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d5862fc1d390e01","agent_id":"a6daf208703aac9a7","session_id":"b1b2271b-4c69-47a7-906c-4aa2a3507a54","uuid":"5ef3d9ae-f8f3-4100-a08e-a3e43c3c08ab","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:52:45.972Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad77371189845d80","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
