ical_path_length to 4.\n\nWait — but is adding the edge the best fix, or rewording? Let me read E001 and E002 to decide. Actually let me also read the other epics to check priority inheritance: adding E001 (P0) → E002 (P0) doesn't break priority inheritance. Both are Implementation types; Rules 7/8/10 concern konflux/license/repo onboarding — not applicable here, so no parallel-edge violation.\n\nLet me read the epic files.","signature":"73a1969af2c04db3a9f9d8db57421505"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":16237,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d5862fc1d390e01","agent_id":"a6daf208703aac9a7","session_id":"b1b2271b-4c69-47a7-906c-4aa2a3507a54","uuid":"1f899215-dae2-4eac-9349-f599b3c64d89","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:52:57.081Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
