{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9b77dd513c31cb9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n3\ttitle: Platform Operator FIPS compliance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: -1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: Medium\n24\tai_implementability_score: 2\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Platform Operator FIPS compliance\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic makes the Platform Operator compliant with the FIPS 140-3 posture of the model serving stack: the operator's own image links only validated cryptographic modules, and the operator correctly deploys and reconciles the serving stack on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters. It produces the operator-side remediation records and test results that feed the compliance evidence package.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Audit the Platform Operator image for linkages to non-validated cryptographic libraries (including transitive dependencies).\n39\t- Remediate findings so the operator image links only validated cryptographic modules.\n40\t- Verify the operator deploys, reconciles, and manages the serving stack (including the FIPS-remediated serving images) on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster.\n41\t- Deliver the operator's module inventory entries, remediation records, and test results for use by the compliance evidence package.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- A module inventory entry set covering the Platform Operator image exists, listing each cryptographic library linkage and its validation status.\n46\t- A scan of the remediated operator image confirms no non-validated cryptographic module is linked.\n47\t- The operator successfully deploys and reconciles the serving stack on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster (CR status reaches Ready for a deployed InferenceService using remediated images).\n48\t- The operator image build is revertible to the prior build (documented rollback path), since this work replaces an existing image build.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the request path) — this epic delivers that for the Platform Operator.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac13f1b5084b4195","agent_id":"ad4a5cc8c8142fa9f","session_id":"b1b2271b-4c69-47a7-906c-4aa2a3507a54","uuid":"0376c89a-d813-4458-8cba-f69d005f65f7","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:54:56.146Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9b77dd513c31cb9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013"}
