n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- The evidence package contains the module inventory, build attestations, and test results for every serving-stack image in scope (KServe components, serving data plane, and Platform Operator).\n48\t- The evidence package is submitted to the security review board at each defined milestone, and board feedback is triaged and addressed.\n49\t- The evidence package is submitted to the external accredited certification laboratory, and its intake/triage status is recorded.\n50\t\n51\t## Risks / Notes\n52\t\n53\t- Certification laboratory turnaround is historically six to nine months, and review-board cadence is externally controlled; neither can be compressed by engineering effort. These are schedule risks, not acceptance conditions — the epic's engineering completion point is the assembled, submitted, and triaged package.\n54\t- The certification outcome and its timing are outside this strategy's control; the engineering compliance value (FIPS-capable images, CI enforcement, documentation) does not depend on it.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac13f1b5084b4195","agent_id":"ad4a5cc8c8142fa9f","session_id":"b1b2271b-4c69-47a7-906c-4aa2a3507a54","uuid":"7e28a982-47b9-413f-8c15-4fc28dc7d7b4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:55:01.082Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-882fdd7471b769ad","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013"}
